{
	title: 'Action resolution carries the session context',
	spec: 'Action resolution knows the session it serves: actions.resolve(text, ctx?) and actions.arrived(call, ctx?) take CallContext { cwd, sessionId, model } and pass it to Tool.action.resolve(raw, ctx?); ToolContext carries the model too. turns.ts supplies it when a call arrives and when it runs, so both resolutions of one call see the same context. Optional where a caller has no session (tests, HELP); hooks treat a missing context as unknown, never as a match. Need: an EDIT quirks plugin applies parser leniency only for the models that need it and logs firings with the model. Context objects are added on the trodden path: to a hookable function only when a real plugin needs it, naming that need in its task; never preemptively.',
